<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:39Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Borussia Dortmund bows to fan pressure and end Rheinmetall deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5df9cf2e091c688b1d24a45d893962f4f9018f460bf328069fcb1f49c20d570f</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T15:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/borussia-dortmund-bows-to-fan-pressure-and-end-rheinmetall-deal/a-79980121--2c9b64a964f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/borussia-dortmund-bows-to-fan-pressure-and-end-rheinmetall-deal/a-79980121?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Borussia Dortmund has reluctantly ended its association with a major sponsor after long-term fan protests. They are not the first Bundesliga club to u-turn, as commercial interests clash with politics and fan culture.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Deutsche Bank under fire after internal documents made public</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cfd9b2e6b06fa5a1b20dd59fcf85524abddebbc0c0f641170ac940e246e498b3</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T18:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/deutsche-bank-under-fire-after-internal-documents-made-public/a-79974543--b2ac12e5d332.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/deutsche-bank-under-fire-after-internal-documents-made-public/a-79974543?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A cache of internal records outlines the bank's dealings with Jeffrey Epstein, Donald Trump and Russian oligarchs. The German lender has sought to deflect criticism by claiming its bad behavior is a thing of the past.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Plans for Rwanda migrant hub come under fire</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a83c314da5f3470adb35c61f927a1d56f1c81f102be8d415dd6f47c1a4c0d60c</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T10:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-plans-for-rwanda-migrant-hub-come-under-fire/live-79965639--9c6685ac3d74.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-plans-for-rwanda-migrant-hub-come-under-fire/live-79965639?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Human rights groups have slammed plans by Germany and four other EU states to send rejected asylum seekers to Rwanda. In other news, business start-ups in Germany are on track to reach the highest level since 2015.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'Coalition of the Willing' meets in Berlin: Europe remains committed to Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ccd6571972095527e32af1a49d088ac9e646538c602ee5c29b97f50efc604b3</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T15:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/coalition-of-the-willing-meets-in-berlin-europe-remains-committed-to-ukraine/a-79974996--9529e6865e8b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/coalition-of-the-willing-meets-in-berlin-europe-remains-committed-to-ukraine/a-79974996?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The "Coalition of the Willing" supporting Ukraine is gathering in Berlin. One of the key issues under discussion is whether Europe will be able to play a role in future negotiations over the country's future.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp and Wirtz offer glimpse of bright German future</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4eb609db7a52fb8d1cb9333b3dc6b71203805198f33ae17ca685cb4f7d56bf1</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T11:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-and-wirtz-offer-glimpse-of-bright-german-future/a-79968184--a5059b3200c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-and-wirtz-offer-glimpse-of-bright-german-future/a-79968184?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's fall from grace in recent years has seen the team drift away from the fans. But Monday's drubbing of the Netherlands and the impact of Jürgen Klopp, Florian Wirtz and emerging youngsters offers hope.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Tesla planning €3BN investment in German factory to produce Cybercabs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd0f23821059ed0086dd03dfa6352701075b8b56e65b9a2b10be536fe46e7c89</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T16:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tesla-planning-_3bn-investment-in-german-factory-to-produce-cybercabs/a-79961416--56a989627169.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tesla-planning-€3bn-investment-in-german-factory-to-produce-cybercabs/a-79961416?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Elon Musk-owned company is looking to further expand its only European production line. Brandenburg's state leader has welcomed the decision.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>The AfD and neo-Nazi networks: How close are the connections?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32d484b124507f057f26b2733e88aa17f1e96b26f74827cdefb90d1ba47e8853</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T16:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-afd-and-neo-nazi-networks-how-close-are-the-connections/a-79961920--fb16f5d74381.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-afd-and-neo-nazi-networks-how-close-are-the-connections/a-79961920?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Alternative for Germany party (AfD) has become a focal point for the far right. Many of its members and staff have ties to ethnonationalist or neo-Nazi organizations.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp wants Infantino out as FIFA candidate deadline looms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dbb7c6c46a17bd745de97024d29acbb76b8c6752a403c112d0ae661cbe6cb874</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T11:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-infantino-out-as-fifa-candidate-deadline-looms/a-79958229--458d3356c9f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-infantino-out-as-fifa-candidate-deadline-looms/a-79958229?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany coach Jürgen Klopp has joined the chorus of football figures critical of FIFA President Gianni Infantino. But with time running out, there are few who seem willing to run against him.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be802f4fbe22400806003fdff8c383adf8ff7b793e01664687487bfe0ae129a9</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
